I think this topic has come up before, but I just died from it, so I 
wanna bring it up again.

A vampire in Slash'em cannot pick up stuff in a pit because "You cannot 
reach the bottom of the pit."
The only way to get the item out of the pit is by either waiting for 
someone else to pick it up, or teleport the item(s) out of the pit or to 
dig downwards, creating a hole. It seems that then you can then fly part 
of the way down the hole to pick up the items that didnt fall through 
your hole (and are now 'levitating'), however you can't do this with an 
ordinary pit.

Pressing : over a pit gives the following message.
"There is a pit here.  You see here a rock." (I dropped a rock in my 
wizmode pit)
You can look into the pit but you cant touch the stuff inside it.
However when you get blinded and press : over a pit then you can touch 
the items in the pit.
"There is a pit here.  You try to feel what is lying here on the 
floor.--More--"
"You feel here a rock."
But you _still_ cant pick up the items in the pit, even though you have 
just touched them.


Guess what I 'felt' in a pit?
